SUMMARY:Scenic Avl Series #1: Hard Times Trail - Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nIf you plan to carpool\, add a com
 ment below.\n\nJoin me for a hike in Bent Creek. We will start at the Hard
  Times trailhead and hike about 6 miles. We will stop to see the exhibit i
 n the visitors center in the Arboretum - 20 minutes.\n\nRating: Moderate\n
 Length: 6 - Hardtimes\, Arboretum\, bigger loop back to cars. If you want 
 to cut it short after the Arboretum\, that's fine\, too.\nSurface: Trail/L
 ogging Road\nElevation Gain: 400-600 ft\nPace: 3.0-3.2 mph\nDogs: on leash
 .\nGear: In winter\, bring a headlamp or flashlight at night. In the summe
 r\, bug spray and water\, depending on the heat.\nBears: None so far this 
 year\, but now is the season for them.\nFeatures: We will go into the Arbo
 retum and look at the Trolls exhibit\, and any other exhibits that interes
 t us.\nCautions: Muddy after rain\, with some high grass in summer. Long p
 ants and bug repellent recommended.\n\nCarpool: If you want to carpool\, p
 lease put a comment below and plan to meet at Papa's and Beer 15 minutes b
 efore the start time\, in front of the restaurant\, two rows back\; carpoo
 l location: [https://maps.app.goo.gl/8oGqteNy2X9dnccS9](https://maps.app.g
 oo.gl/8oGqteNy2X9dnccS9)\nIf there are no comments\, assume no carpool..\n
 \nTrailhead Location\nHard Times Trailhead\n375 Wesley Branch Rd · Ashevi
 lle\, NC\n\nSpring\, summer\, fall and winter daytime route:\n[https://www
 .alltrails.com/explore/map/map-march-14-2024-39ae2ed?u=i&sh=ifwm3x](https:
 //www.alltrails.com/explore/map/map-march-14-2024-39ae2ed?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n
 Alternate Winter Route used at night: [https://www.alltrails.com/explore/m
 ap/hard-times-alternate-37968ad](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/har
 d-times-alternate-37968ad)\n\n[Scenic Asheville Series](https://docs.googl
 e.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?usp
 =drivesdk): There are 9 hikes in the series\; hike them all and receive an
  attractive badge for your backpack. Check your progress here: [Hiker Spre
 adsheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37c
 Al4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0). **Special perk for badge holders:** 
 You can always come on the hike\, even if you are on the waitlist.\n.\n\nR
 SVP and On-Time Start:\n\n*There is no cell coverage at the start of the h
 ike. If you are late\, we will leave on time because we can't see last-min
 ute texts or comments.\n- Please change your RSVP as soon as you know you 
 can't make it.\n\nNO Guests: Please ask guests to sign up for the hike the
 mselves.\n\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves h
 iking which may be on natural trails with typical hazards or on city stree
 ts that may have traffic. Participants are responsible for their safety on
  streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a p
 rofessional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this 
 trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you
  freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\
 , and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this eve
 nt. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [htt
 ps://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
